protG-T16-F-linear-dozens-bcxs_charmm - this runs the folded side of site
saturation point mutations at T16 in protein G. This uses the linear loss
function, bcxs bias, and the dozens of substituents fnex implicit constraint.

Make a copy of the examples/engine/charmm or examples/engine/bladelib templates
and copy this directory into it, renaming it prep, and editing the path in
alf_info.py 'enginepath' to point to your charmm executable. Expected results
after production are in a file called Result.txt .

Note the loss function, bias, and implicit constraints choices are suboptimal.
This exmples serves to illustrate how to select those options in alf_info.py .
Successfully converging results will require significantly more effort than the
default protocol found in examples/engine/charmm. An easier to converge variant
with only hydrophobic mutations is available in Fpart.
